title: attach on an exited container destroys its exit status on Podman
updated: 2026-08-27T18:34:37Z
---

Measured 2026-08-27 on rootless Podman 5.4.2 (API 1.41) and Docker 29.7.2
(API 1.55), isolated with a controlled before/after probe:

  PODMAN  before attach   inspect=[exited 4]   wait={"StatusCode":4,"Error":null}
  PODMAN  after  attach   inspect=[created 0]  wait={"StatusCode":-1,"Error":null}
  DOCKER  before attach   inspect=[exited 4]   wait={"StatusCode":4}
  DOCKER  after  attach   inspect=[exited 4]   wait={"StatusCode":4}

Attaching to an already-exited container on Podman reverts it to
Status: created, resets ExitCode to 0, and makes a subsequent wait answer
StatusCode -1 -- a sentinel inside a 200 with no error signalled anywhere.

It is NOT the hang that does it. The call itself does. All three variants
trigger it:
  - stream=1&logs=1  (hangs, then destroys)
  - stream=1 alone   (hangs, then destroys)
  - stream=0&logs=1  (closes in 2ms, and still destroys)

GET /containers/{id}/logs does NOT do it. Docker does not do it.

This matters more than it looks: karr #52 changed containers->attach to
default to stream=0, logs=1 precisely because that variant returns cleanly.
It returns cleanly and still destroys the exit status. So the new default
made attach fast and left it destructive.

containers->attach is therefore a DATA-LOSS operation on Podman against a
stopped container, not merely an awkward one. A caller that attaches to
collect output and then asks wait for the exit code gets -1 and has no way
to recover the real value -- the engine no longer holds it.

To decide:
  - the POD must say this outright, and say it where a reader looks before
    calling attach, not in a caveat section
  - whether containers->attach should refuse against a non-running container
    on Podman, or warn, or do nothing but document
  - whether entity API::Docker::Container->attach needs the same treatment
  - whether this is worth reporting upstream to Podman; it looks like a bug
    rather than a documented divergence

Related: #52 (the hang, now known to affect Docker equally), #45 (stats),
#50 (croak text). The theme is the same -- attach and stats are where both
engines behave worst.
